  "body": "Four whole-helper placements improve the currently selected PR1094 T16 packing from conditional **\u03ba = 0.001672660197076918** to **0.001672664045494084** (+0.000230077643548%). The local R480 supplier, widths, 144-call order, physical stock and bit supplier are unchanged.\n\nA two-move vacancy path exposes an eight-slot suffix; two width-four helpers from distinct calls fill it. The complete profile changes by `H7 - 2 H3 - H1 < 0` for every `Hr = r^p`, `0 < p < 1`. Only four of 69,120 owner rows change. `MOVES.json` gives every before/after row, and `build.py` reconstructs the data and bindings without an optimizer.\n\nValidation:\n\n- The unchanged strict T16 verifier passes all 11 stages, including fresh controller emission, audit and finite invoice; 69 admission, 12 bit, 15 controller and six independent owner rejection controls pass.\n- Both exact moment engines and 47 strict outer inequalities per native/conservative assembly pass. The complete published wrapper also passes locally on CPython 3.14.8; registered Python 3.12 CI is declared.\n- All 278 external inputs are pinned and declared for CI invalidation. Frozen predecessors are unchanged. Native local ancestry is source-bound reuse, not a new cold rebuild. Package metadata and diff checks pass.\n\nThis is an improvement to the **selected PR1094 benchmark**, not the best known packing of that supplier. [PR1407](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1407) already reports **\u03ba = 0.001672680818492982** for the same unchanged supplier; this PR provides a compact four-row alternative. The two patches overlap at owner rows2010 and34306 and affected bins, so they cannot be composed as written. PR1154, PR1992 and PR2044 also report higher values for changed suppliers or transfer assumptions. All inherited all-size/compiler, realization, hosting, precision/tape, recovery, analytic and bit H1-H5 assumptions remain; no unconditional theorem or global packing optimum is claimed. The selected certificate is not edited.\n\n[philippeVV's independent review](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2077#issuecomment-6176996271), with disclosed Claude assistance, reports full CPython3.12 strict/registered replay and metadata-check passes, plus a separate seed67 owner audit with eleven rejection controls and no blocking finding. The package now explicitly states that offsets reserve static disjoint prefix slices; their order need not match the unchanged call chronology.\n\nReproduce from a complete checkout:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/complex-t16-vacancy-chain/verify.py --work /absolute/fresh/output\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/complex-t16-vacancy-chain --check-only\n```\n\nPrepared for George Lydakis with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance and coordination with Ody. Predecessor attribution and exact source lineage are retained in the package. Fresh overlap search covered 347 open PRs and 723 discussion records with complete pagination; this is not a novelty certificate.\n",
